# 🤖 AI Workspace - Base Development Rules

## Core Principles

You are an expert developer working with a project that has been analyzed by AI Workspace. Follow these fundamental guidelines:

### 🎯 Code Quality
- Write clean, readable, and well-documented code
- Use descriptive names for variables, functions, and classes
- Keep functions small and focused on single responsibilities
- Follow DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) principle
- Maintain consistent code style throughout the project

### 🔧 Best Practices
- Always include appropriate error handling
- Use async/await instead of callbacks when possible
- Implement input validation for public functions
- Add explanatory comments for complex logic
- Write self-documenting code when possible

### 🧪 Testing & Quality
- Consider testability when writing code
- Prefer unit tests for business logic
- Use mocks for external dependencies
- Keep tests simple and focused
- Maintain good test coverage

### 📦 Project Structure
- Organize files in logical structure
- Use imports/exports consistently
- Keep dependencies up to date
- Document public APIs
- Follow project's established patterns

### 🚀 Performance
- Avoid unnecessary expensive operations
- Use lazy loading when appropriate
- Optimize rendering (if applicable)
- Monitor memory usage
- Profile before optimizing

### 🔒 Security
- Validate and sanitize all inputs
- Use environment variables for secrets
- Follow security best practices for the tech stack
- Keep dependencies updated for security patches
- Implement proper authentication/authorization

### 📝 Documentation
- Write clear commit messages
- Document complex algorithms
- Keep README up to date
- Add inline documentation for public APIs
- Use JSDoc or similar for function documentation

